Grow the event loop's fixed-base pointer arrays instead of overflowing them.

timers, active_deferrals and active_events were allocated at a fixed 256-entry
capacity whose max_* field was never consulted, so an insert past 256 wrote
past the allocation.  Each array is addressed only through its evpl->* field by
index, with no cached base pointer and no stored back-index, so a realloc that
moves the buffer is observed on the next index.  A shared helper,
evpl_loop_array_grow(), doubles the capacity on exhaustion (updating the
matching max_* field so it becomes the live capacity) and computes the new
element count and byte size in size_t, aborting rather than wrapping before the
value is narrowed to evpl_realloc's unsigned int size argument.

evpl_timer_insert() and evpl_defer() grow in place; the five active-events
append sites are funnelled through a single evpl_active_event_append() helper
that performs the same check in one place.

